  "summary": "MRCL2Suhail exfiltrates working-directory file listing on import to pinggy tunnel host",
  "details": "On `import MRCL2Suhail`, top-level code in core.py (reached via __init__.py) enumerates the current working directory with os.listdir('.') and sends the resulting file listing over a raw TCP socket to the hardcoded host hyhui-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link on port 35957. The destination is a pinggy.link ephemeral tunnel fronting the IP 13.205.45.209 embedded in the hostname, unrelated to the package's advertised 'Document integrity utility' purpose. The package ships no functionality matching that description; the import-time network beacon is its only observable behavior.",
